-- title:
--   Regularity at w of differentials of functions from the smaller field
-- statement:
--   Let $K, F, K', F'$ be fields, with $F$ a $K$-algebra, $F'$ a $K'$-algebra, $K'$ a $K$-algebra, and $F'$ an algebra over both $F$ and $K$, the scalar towers $K \to K' \to F'$ and $K \to F \to F'$ being compatible; assume $K$ and $K'$ algebraically closed, $F'$ essentially of finite type over $K'$, and both $F/K$ and $F'/K'$ curves in the sense of `IsCurveOver`: every nonzero function has a principal divisor of degree $0$, every place has residue field finite over the base field, and the module of Kähler differentials is free of rank one over the function field. Three further hypotheses are assumed: the existence of $x_0 \in F$ transcendental over $K$ with $F$ finite and separable over $K(x_0)$; the existence of $x \in F'$ transcendental over $K'$ with $F'$ finite over $K'(x)$; and that the $K'$-subfield of $F'$ generated by the image of $F$ is all of $F'$. Let $w$ be a place of $F'/K'$, i.e. a valuation subring $\mathcal{O}_w \subsetneq F'$ containing the image of $K'$ and a principal ideal ring, and suppose that $\mathcal{O}_w$ contains the image of every element of $F$. Then for every $x \in F$ the differential $\mathrm{d}(\mathrm{algebraMap}\,x) \in \Omega_{F'/K'}$ is regular at $w$: it equals $f \cdot \mathrm{d}\pi_w$ for some $f \in \mathcal{O}_w$, where $\pi_w$ is the chosen uniformizer of $w$.
--
--   This is the statement that, under a constant field extension with algebraically closed constants, the differentials of functions coming from the smaller field have no pole at a place of $F'$ lying over the generic point of the curve over $K$ (those places at which all of $F$ is integral). It is used by [`AlgebraicCurve.isRegularAt_map_of_forall_isRegularAt_of_constantFieldExtension_of_isAlgClosed`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.isRegularAt_map_of_forall_isRegularAt_of_constantFieldExtension_of_isAlgClosed) and [`AlgebraicCurve.map_mem_polarDifferentials_of_constantFieldExtension_of_isAlgClosed`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.map_mem_polarDifferentials_of_constantFieldExtension_of_isAlgClosed), which compare regular and polar differentials along the base change.
